# Data layout (the same as data-liberation's project template):
#   data/original/   immutable originals, never edited in place
#   data/processed/  tidy outputs, regenerated by the pipeline
#   data/audit/      audit and reconcile reports (committed: they are the evidence PRs review)
#   data/lookups/    hand-maintained crosswalks and vocabularies (committed)
#
# Where originals live is the storage-budget decision in Outline section 2; record it in
# decision-log.md. Default below: bulk, re-downloadable originals are ignored, and their hash
# and URL in data/processed/provenance.csv let the pipeline fetch them again. If you commit
# them (or keep them in Git LFS), delete the data/original/* line.
data/original/*
!data/**/.gitkeep
# Curated source of record (small, hand-made: the project's actual asset) is TRACKED, never
# ignored. Uncomment and point at the real file; for files in subdirectories also un-ignore
# each parent directory. Document it as immutable in docs/data-dictionary.md.
# !data/original/catalog.csv
# !data/original/<source>/
# !data/original/<source>/<file>

# Processed outputs: commit small CSVs if the project publishes from the repository; keep large
# or binary outputs out of history (GitHub rejects files over 100 MB).
data/processed/*.parquet
data/processed/*.db

# Large / binary artifacts (use object storage or Git LFS instead)
*.feather
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.pkl
*.joblib
*.sqlite
*.db

# Secrets and credentials — never commit
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
credentials.json
secrets.yaml
# OpenSharing recipient profile holds a bearer token; commit only the .example
opensharing/share-profile.json

# Notebook cruft — clear outputs before committing
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*-checkpoint.ipynb

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
